      scenario: 'Zava Group is a diversified ASEAN conglomerate operating across 11 divisions — chemicals, agribusiness, manufacturing, financial services, properties, BPO, trading, pharma, healthcare, retail and group treasury — with about 8,400 employees in Malaysia, Indonesia and Singapore. The Group is dual-listed on Bursa Malaysia (Group HoldCo) and IDX (the Indonesian operating company), with treasury operations spanning MYR (functional currency for Group reporting) and IDR (Indonesian operating ledger; FX rate ≈ 1 MYR : 3,580 IDR). FY2025 EBITDA missed budget by 18%, three divisions are now in negative EBITDA, the Securities Commission Malaysia and Otoritas Jasa Keuangan (OJK) Indonesia have both requested clarifications, and lead relationship banks (CIMB, Maybank, Mandiri, BCA) have raised covenant questions. The Group CEO walks into an emergency Board review in 48 hours and needs a defensible briefing pack, divisional variance analysis, regulator and lender holding lines (covering BNM/Bursa AND OJK/BEI), and a 30-day corrective programme — fast.',
