      taglineBM: 'Curtailment pada 8.6%, kos O&M naik 14% dan tempoh pembiayaan semula RM1.4B — semakan pipeline Lembaga Pengarah Khamis.',
      scenarioBM: 'Zava Tenaga Boleh Baharu Malaysia ialah IPP tenaga boleh baharu Malaysiayang tersenarai di ASEAN Stock Exchange dengan kira-kira 1,900 pekerja dan kapasiti operasi solar serta angin 1.4 GW, ditambah pipeline pembangunan projek rentas sempadan 850 MW dengan gabungan Indonesia yang tersenarai di ASEAN Stock Exchange. Data operasi menunjukkan Solar Generation dan Wind Farm Output skala utiliti hampir kepada nameplate, tetapi Grid Curtailment Tracker mendedahkan curtailment telah mencapai 8.6% di dua tapak kerana kekangan transmisi utiliti nasional dan had dispatch utiliti Indonesia di Sumatra. PPA Revenue Tracker menunjukkan ketirisan hasil sekitar RM41 juta sepanjang empat suku tahun lalu, sementara O&M Cost Summary meningkat 14% tahun ke tahun disebabkan penggantian inverter, pemeriksaan blade dan alat ganti import. Pipeline Indonesia 850 MW bergantung pada rundingan semula PPA utiliti Indonesia, penjajaran Renewable Portfolio Standard dan permit alam sekitar daripada pihak berkuasa Indonesia, dan tempoh pembiayaan semula RM1.4 bilion bermula dalam 14 minggu. Suruhanjaya Tenaga dan Kementerian Tenaga dan Sumber Mineral Indonesia kedua-duanya memantau prestasi dispatch, dan Lembaga Pengarah mahukan bukti lebih jelas bahawa rancangan asset management serta pendedahan ESG mampu bertahan di bawah penelitian pemberi pinjaman. Ketua Pegawai Eksekutif Kumpulan telah memanggil semakan pipeline Lembaga Pengarah pada Khamis dan memerlukan rancangan pemulihan yang boleh dipertahankan untuk curtailment, kos O&M, project finance dan engagement pengawal selia — dengan pantas.',
      companyIDEN: 'Zava Renewables Indonesia',
      taglineIDEN: 'Curtailment at 8.6%, O&M cost up 14% and an IDR 4.8 trillion refinancing window — Board pipeline review Thursday.',
      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Renewables Indonesia is an Indonesian renewable energy IPP listed on the ASEAN Stock Exchange with about 2,300 employees and 1.4 GW of operating solar and wind capacity, plus an 850 MW cross-border project development pipeline with a Malaysian partner. Operating data shows utility-scale Solar Generation and Wind Farm Output close to nameplate, but the Grid Curtailment Tracker shows curtailment reaching 8.6% at two locations because of state-utility dispatch limits in Sumatra and Malaysian utility transmission constraints. PPA Revenue Tracker shows revenue leakage of around IDR 145 billion over the last four quarters, while O&M Cost Summary is up 14% year on year because of inverter replacements, blade inspections and imported spare parts. The 850 MW pipeline depends on state-utility PPA renegotiation, Renewable Portfolio Standard alignment and Environment and Forestry Ministry environmental permits, while the IDR 4.8 trillion refinancing window opens in 14 weeks. The Energy and Mineral Resources Ministry and the Energy Commission are both monitoring dispatch performance, and the Board wants clearer evidence that the asset management plan and ESG disclosures can withstand lender scrutiny. The CEO is holding a Board pipeline review on Thursday and needs a defensible recovery plan for curtailment, O&M cost, project finance and regulator engagement — fast.',
