          prompts: [
            {
              label: 'Group P&L → Interactive Strategy App — 3-step fan-out',
              text: 'STEP 1 — Understand + build the app.  I\'ve attached Contoso\'s FY27 group plan model. First walk me through the structure — divisions, drivers, intercompany eliminations, and any assumptions Strategy will have to defend at the September board.  Then convert into a Python program with an interactive HTML front-end: - Sliders: primary output USD/T (750–1,250), EUR/USD (1.05–1.15), specialty-chem EBITDA margin (8–18%), property pre-sale velocity (60–110% of plan), opex inflation (0–6%). - Show: Group revenue, Group EBITDA, Group PAT, division contribution waterfall, EBITDA bridge vs FY26, board-level scorecard.  Deliver runnable Python plus a self-contained HTML I can preview locally.  STEP 2 — Validate + run scenarios.  Run the new app at the original plan assumptions. Produce a parity report against the spreadsheet (revenue, EBITDA, PAT by division, group total) — flag any divergence > USD 1m.  Then run three scenarios: - Base (current plan). - Bull: primary output USD 1,200, USD 4.30, specialty-chem margin 16%, property pre-sale 105%. - Bear: primary output USD 850, USD 4.65, specialty-chem margin 9%, property pre-sale 75%.  Summarise EBITDA swing, the top three division/driver combinations driving variance, and identify the one assumption the bear scenario hinges on.  STEP 3 — Strategy off-site pack.  Build a 10-slide deck titled "FY27 Plan — Sensitivity Pack for Strategy Off-site": 1. Cover 2. Scenario table 3. EBITDA bridge 4. Division contribution waterfall 5. Sensitivity heatmap (primary output × FX) 6. Bear-case kill switch 7. Property pre-sale sensitivity 8. Specialty Chemicals margin sensitivity 9. Decisions required 10. Appendix.  Save to /Group/Strategy/FY27_Offsite/. Apply the "Confidential — Board Pack" sensitivity label.'
            }
          ],
