      taglineBM: 'RevPAR merosot di dua resort utama, komisen OTA menekan margin, dan tunggakan Capex bertemu pertikaian asset-management pemilik.',
      scenarioBM: 'Zava Hotels Malaysia ialah kumpulan hospitaliti tersenarai di Malaysia yang mengendalikan 14 hartanah merentasi Indonesia (Bali, Lombok, Yogyakarta, the regional capital, Bintan), Malaysia dan Vietnam — gabungan aset milik sendiri, pajakan dan diurus pihak ketiga berjumlah 3,800 bilik serta 9 outlet F&B setiap kluster. RevPAR kumpulan turun 11% pada suku terakhir, dua resort utama di Bali dan Lombok berada 14-18% di belakang belanjawan RevPAR, komisen OTA meningkat daripada 18% kepada 23% hasil bilik bersih selepas perubahan re-tier terbaharu oleh dua OTA terbesar, tunggakan Capex penyelenggaraan di tiga hartanah kini ditanda Merah dalam audit standard jenama oleh Kementerian Pelancongan dan juruaudit francais, pemilik dua hartanah terurus mencetuskan pertikaian asset-management berkaitan yuran pengurusan dan kadar renovasi, dan ASEAN Stock Exchange telah meminta penjelasan selepas pendedahan berkaitan OTA yang tajam daripada kumpulan setara serantau. Data ketibaan pelancongan agensi statistik menunjukkan permintaan domestik jarak dekat melemah menjelang shoulder September. Pengarah Urusan Kumpulan akan menghadiri semakan komersial dan asset-management Lembaga Pengarah dalam 7 hari. Pengarah Urusan memerlukan pakej taklimat operasi dan komersial yang dapat dipertahankan, varians RevPAR mengikut hartanah, bridge komisen OTA, rancangan keutamaan semula Capex, kenyataan pegangan pemilik, serta program penstabilan komersial dan jenama 90 hari.',
      companyIDEN: 'Zava Hotels Indonesia',
      taglineIDEN: 'RevPAR weakens at two flagship resorts, OTA commissions squeeze margin, and a Capex backlog meets an owner asset-management dispute.',
      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Hotels Indonesia is a hospitality group operating 14 properties in Indonesia (Bali, Lombok, Yogyakarta, the regional capital, Bintan), Malaysia, and Vietnam — a mix of owned, leased, and third-party managed assets totalling 3,800 rooms and 9 F&B outlets per cluster. Group RevPAR fell 11% in the last quarter, two flagship resorts in Bali and Lombok are operating 14-18% below the RevPAR corporate budget, OTA commissions rose from 18% to 23% of net room revenue after the latest re-tier changes by the two largest OTAs, the maintenance Capex backlog at three properties is now flagged Red in brand-standards audits by the Tourism Ministry and franchise auditor, the owner of two managed properties triggered an asset-management dispute over management fees and renovation pacing, and ASEAN Stock Exchange requested clarification after a sharp OTA-related disclosure from a regional peer. Statistics Agency tourism-arrivals data show domestic short-haul demand softening into the September shoulder. The Group CEO will lead a Board commercial and asset-management review in 7 days. The CEO needs a defensible operations and commercial briefing pack, property-by-property RevPAR variance, OTA commission bridge, Capex reprioritisation plan, owner statements, and a 90-day commercial and brand stabilisation programme.',
