      taglineBM: 'Hab utama pada 112% kapasiti; penemuan ICAO dan DKPPU belum ditutup; semakan tarif tertangguh.',
      scenarioBM: 'Zava Lapangan Terbang Malaysia dan Zava Lapangan Terbang Indonesia beroperasi sebagai pengendali lapangan terbang tahap satu merentasi 14 hab di Malaysia dan Indonesia dengan hasil tahunan RM 4.2 bilion dan kira-kira 9,800 kakitangan langsung. Hab utama beroperasi pada 112% daripada kapasiti reka bentuk, semakan tarif aeronautik telah tertangguh 18 bulan di Kementerian Pengangkutan dan mengekang perancangan hasil FY2026, ICAO telah mengeluarkan 14 penemuan di bawah audit USOAP terkini termasuk 4 penemuan keutamaan mengenai respons kecemasan, DKPPU telah membuka semakan kelayakan udara terhadap 2 subunit pengendalian kargo, pertikaian peruntukan slot dengan 3 syarikat penerbangan tambang rendah terbesar semakin memuncak menjadi aduan rasmi, dan program capex peluasan terminal melebihi peruntukan asal sebanyak 24%. Jawatankuasa capex dan keselamatan Lembaga Pengarah bermesyuarat dalam 21 hari dan pengurusan mesti menunjukkan bahawa kapasiti, keselamatan dan ekonomi tarif adalah selaras sebelum tranche capex seterusnya dilepaskan.',
      companyIDEN: 'Zava Airports Indonesia',
      taglineIDEN: 'Flagship hub at 112% capacity; ICAO and airworthiness-directorate findings open; tariff revision delayed.',
      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Airports Indonesia and Zava Airports Malaysia operate as a tier-one airport operator across 14 hubs in Indonesia and Malaysia with IDR 14.3 trillion in annual revenue and roughly 9,800 direct staff. The flagship hub is operating at 112% of design capacity, aeronautical-services tariff revision has been delayed 18 months at the Ministry of Transportation and is constraining FY2026 revenue planning, ICAO has issued 14 findings in the latest USOAP audit including 4 priority findings on emergency response, the Directorate of Airworthiness and Aircraft Operations has opened an airworthiness review on 2 cargo handling sub-units, slot-allocation disputes with the 3 largest low-cost airlines are escalating into formal complaints, and the terminal expansion capex programme is 24% over the original envelope. The Board Capex and Safety Committee meets in 21 days and management must demonstrate that capacity, safety, and tariff economics are aligned before further capex tranches are released.',
      subsidiaries: [
        'Malaysia Airports Holdings',
        'Angkasa Pura I/II (peer)'
      ],
