      scenarioBM: 'Zava Pelaburan Malaysia ialah Syarikat Pelaburan Berkaitan Kerajaan Malaysia yang mengurus AUM RM 52.4B merentasi ekuiti tersenarai (RM 28B), pasaran swasta (RM 11B), infrastruktur (RM 7B) dan pegangan strategik (RM 6.4B). Dana ini beroperasi di bawah 6 mandat Kementerian: pemeliharaan modal, sasaran pulangan sebenar CPI tambah 4 peratus, agihan dividen kepada Perbendaharaan Persekutuan, lantai ESG berkuat kuasa 2025, sokongan kecairan domestik, dan stewardship ke atas 9 pegangan strategik. NAV FY2025 ketinggalan penanda aras dasar sebanyak 9.2 peratus — seretan NAV sebanyak RM 1.8B berbanding bogey — didorong terutamanya oleh 3 pegangan strategik (Bumi Energi, Tenaga Nusa Telekom, Pelabuhan Niaga Holdings). Agihan dividen kepada Perbendaharaan meleset daripada sasaran sebanyak 22 peratus (RM 880M sebenar berbanding sasaran RM 1.13B). Audit Dalaman menutup FY2025 dengan 12 penemuan tadbir urus mengenai pengecualian konflik kepentingan, pematuhan mandat dan saringan ESG. Jawatankuasa Kira-kira Wang Negara telah memanggil Ketua Pegawai Pelaburan. Kementerian Kewangan telah meminta pek taklimat 14 hari meliputi pemulihan, penjajaran mandat, pemulihan dividen dan rancangan pemulihan NAV 36 bulan.',
      companyIDEN: 'Zava Investment Indonesia',
      taglineIDEN: 'FY2025 portfolio NAV underperformed benchmark by 9.2% — Ministry briefing in 14 days.',
      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Investment Indonesia is an Indonesian Government-Linked Investment Company managing AUM of IDR 832 trillion across listed equities (IDR 448 trillion), private markets (IDR 176 trillion), infrastructure (IDR 112 trillion), and strategic holdings (IDR 102 trillion). The Fund operates under 6 Ministry mandates: capital preservation, real return target of CPI plus 4 percent, dividend distribution to the State Treasury, ESG floor effective 2025, domestic liquidity support, and stewardship over 9 strategic holdings. FY2025 NAV underperformed the policy benchmark by 9.2 percent — a NAV gap of IDR 28 trillion against the bogey — driven mainly by 3 strategic holdings (Bumi Energi Persero, Zava Telco Indonesia, Pelabuhan Niaga Holdings). Dividend distribution to the State Treasury missed target by 22 percent (IDR 14 trillion actual vs IDR 18 trillion target). Internal Audit closed FY2025 with 12 governance findings on conflict-of-interest waivers, mandate compliance, and ESG screening. House Commission VI has summoned the Chief Investment Officer. The Ministry of State-Owned Enterprises has requested a 14-day briefing pack covering remediation, mandate alignment, dividend recovery, and a 36-month NAV restoration plan.',
