      geo: 'MY',
      companyBM: 'Pengawal Selia Kewangan Zava Malaysia',
      taglineBM: 'Pelanggaran broker-dealer Tier-2 terdedah — keputusan penguatkuasaan penyeliaan dalam 5 hari.',
      scenarioBM: 'Pengawal Selia Kewangan Zava Malaysia (SKM) ialah pihak berkuasa berkanun yang menyelia 142 pengantara pasaran modal: 38 broker-dealer, 27 pengurus dana, 41 penjaga aset, 36 penasihat — gabungan aset pelanggan RM 412B. SKM mengendalikan rangka kerja penyeliaan 4 teras: ambang kehematan (kecukupan modal, kecairan, leveraj), peraturan kelakuan pasaran, jangkaan ESG dan tadbir urus, serta perancangan resolusi. Titan Capital Sdn Bhd ialah broker-dealer Tier-2 yang memegang RM 21B aset pelanggan. Dalam 30 hari lepas Titan telah melanggar 3 ambang kehematan (Capital Adequacy Ratio jatuh kepada 7.8 peratus berbanding lantai 12 peratus, Liquidity Coverage Ratio jatuh kepada 91 peratus berbanding lantai 110 peratus, Aggregate Indebtedness meningkat kepada 14.2x berbanding siling 10x), menjual produk berstruktur berleveraj kepada pelanggan runcit yang kelihatan melanggar peraturan kesesuaian, dan lewat mendedahkan insiden siber yang menjejaskan 11,200 akaun pelanggan — didedahkan 19 hari selepas dikesan berbanding peraturan 72 jam. Suruhanjaya SKM mesti memutuskan dalam 5 hari sama ada untuk membatalkan lesen, menggantung dagangan, mengeluarkan arahan pemulihan, atau meningkatkannya kepada siasatan jenayah. Dua pengawal selia rakan setara (MAS dan ASEAN Financial Services Authority) telah meminta read-across secara peribadi memandangkan Titan mengendalikan entiti tempahan di Singapura. Penelitian Jawatankuasa Kira-kira Wang Negara dan perhatian Ketua Audit Negara dijangka.',
      companyIDEN: 'Zava Financial Regulator Indonesia',
      taglineIDEN: 'Tier-2 securities-firm breach exposed — supervisory enforcement decision in 5 days.',
      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Financial Regulator Indonesia (ASEAN Financial Services Authority) is the statutory authority overseeing 142 capital-market intermediaries: 38 securities firms, 27 investment managers, 41 custodians, 36 advisers — total client assets of IDR 6,560 trillion. ASEAN Financial Services Authority runs a 4-pillar supervisory framework: prudential thresholds (capital adequacy, liquidity, leverage), market-conduct rules, ESG and governance expectations, and resolution planning. Titan Capital Securities is a Tier-2 securities firm holding IDR 336 trillion in client assets. In the past 30 days Titan has breached 3 prudential thresholds (Capital Adequacy Ratio fell to 7.8 percent vs a 12 percent floor, Liquidity Coverage Ratio fell to 91 percent vs a 110 percent floor, Aggregate Indebtedness rose to 14.2x vs a 10x ceiling), sold leveraged structured products to retail clients in apparent breach of suitability rules, and disclosed late a cyber incident affecting 11,200 client accounts — disclosed 19 days after detection vs the 72-hour rule. The ASEAN Financial Services Authority Board of Commissioners must decide within 5 days whether to revoke the licence, suspend trading, issue a remedial order, or escalate to criminal investigation. Two peer regulators (MAS and BSP) have privately requested read-across given Titan operates a Singapore booking entity. House Commission XI scrutiny and Audit Board attention are expected.',
