      geo: 'MY+ID',
      companyBM: 'Zava Motors',
      taglineBM: 'Kekurangan EV-mix Toyota + rundingan semula prinsipal Honda + 8 pengedar berprestasi rendah — ExCo Kumpulan dalam 14 hari.',
      scenarioBM: 'Zava Motors ialah platform pengedaran dan pengedar automotif Kumpulan dengan hak pengedar tunggal untuk kenderaan penumpang Toyota dan Honda di Malaysia, rangkaian 3S Hyundai berlesen di Indonesia, serta perkongsian jenama elektrik BYD yang baru dimeterai (BEV + PHEV). Kumpulan mengendalikan 92 outlet jualan dan servis di kedua-dua negara (54 di Malaysia, 38 di Indonesia), memasang model CKD terpilih di loji Pekan dan Bekasi, serta menjalankan cabang pembiayaan automotif captive. Tiga tekanan bertembung serentak: (1) sasaran BEV-mix 2027 Toyota Motor Asia Pacific memerlukan 30% jualan elektrik tetapi Zava Motors berada pada 4.1% YTD, dengan penyusunan semula keutamaan capex FY2026 diperlukan antara pelancaran BYD dan barisan hibrid Honda; (2) Honda Motor Co. membuka rundingan semula margin prinsipal yang mahu mengurangkan margin ATPM/pengedar sebanyak 150 bps, mengancam EBITDA FY2026 sebanyak RM 84 juta; (3) 8 daripada 92 pengedar beroperasi di bawah titik pulang modal selama 4 suku berturut-turut — jualan kedai sama turun 11% YoY, kadar attach F&I pada 38% berbanding penanda aras 55%. Pengarah Urusan Kumpulan memerlukan pek sedia ExCo Kumpulan dalam 14 hari merangkumi senario pemulihan EV-mix, pertahanan rundingan semula prinsipal, rancangan rasionalisasi pengedar dan nota taklimat dasar EEV MITI / PPnBM ASEAN Industry Ministry. Rangka rujukan: kumpulan pengedar automotif serantau berbilang jenama yang sebanding.',
      companyIDEN: 'Zava Motors',
      taglineIDEN: 'Toyota EV-mix shortfall + Honda principal renegotiation + 8 underperforming dealers — Group ExCo in 14 days.',
      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Motors is the Group automotive distribution and dealership platform with sole-distributor rights for Toyota and Honda passenger vehicles in Malaysia, an authorised Hyundai 3S network in Indonesia, and a newly signed BYD electrified brand partnership (BEV + PHEV). The Group operates 92 sales-and-service outlets across both countries (54 in Malaysia, 38 in Indonesia), assembles selected CKD models at the Pekan and Bekasi plants, and runs a captive auto-financing unit. Three pressures converge at once: (1) Toyota Motor Asia Pacific 2027 BEV-mix target requires 30% electrified sales but Zava Motors is at 4.1% YTD, with FY2026 capex re-prioritisation needed between the BYD rollout and the Honda hybrid line; (2) Honda Motor Co. opened a principal-margin renegotiation seeking a 150 bps cut to ATPM/distributor margin, threatening Rp 300 billion of FY2026 EBITDA; (3) 8 of 92 dealers are operating below break-even for 4 consecutive quarters — same-store sales down 11% YoY, F&I attach rate at 38% versus a 55% benchmark. The Group Managing Director needs a Group-ExCo-ready pack in 14 days covering EV-mix recovery scenarios, principal-renegotiation defence, dealer-rationalisation plan, and MITI EEV / ASEAN Industry Ministry PPnBM-policy briefing notes. Reference frame: comparable multi-brand regional automotive distribution groups.',
