      taglineBM: 'Peleraian lindung nilai bahan api jet RM 180 juta + gangguan laluan open-skies ASEAN + pertikaian kru kabin pra-Hari Raya — ExCo Kumpulan dalam 10 hari.',
      scenarioBM: 'Zava Air ialah kumpulan penerbangan ASEAN perkhidmatan penuh + tambang rendah dengan hab di the regional capital (Malaysia) dan the regional capital (Indonesia), mengendalikan 78 pesawat narrowbody dan 14 pesawat widebody merentasi 64 destinasi. Tiga tekanan bertembung: (1) buku lindung nilai bahan api jet dileraikan pada Q1 dengan unjuran kerugian RM 180 juta apabila backwardation Brent menolak jurang realisasi berbanding hedged kepada USD 22/bbl; (2) peruntukan open-skies ASEAN baharu menyerahkan slot di laluan utama the regional capital–the regional capital, the regional capital–Singapore dan the regional capital–Phuket kepada pesaing, dengan hakisan yield 8-12% diunjurkan pada 14 laluan; (3) kesatuan kru kabin mengemukakan pertikaian mengenai rostering dan bayaran puncak Hari Raya 18 hari sebelum musim perayaan, mewujudkan risiko tindakan industri pada 12 hari ber-yield tertinggi tahun ini. Pengarah Urusan Kumpulan memerlukan pek ExCo dalam 10 hari merangkumi cash burn lindung nilai bahan api, respons penstrukturan semula rangkaian, pek pengawal selia CAAM/DGCA/MAVCOM dan taklimat rundingan kru kabin. Rangka rujukan: kumpulan penerbangan ASEAN perkhidmatan penuh dan tambang rendah yang sebanding, dengan pengawal selia penerbangan serantau aktif secara serentak.',
      companyIDEN: 'Zava Air',
      taglineIDEN: 'Fuel-hedge unwind Rp 644 billion + ASEAN open-skies route disruption + cabin-crew dispute pre-Hari Raya — Group ExCo in 10 days.',
      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Air is an ASEAN full-service + low-cost carrier group with hubs in the regional capital (Malaysia) and the regional capital (Indonesia), operating 78 narrowbody and 14 widebody aircraft across 64 destinations. Three pressures converge: (1) the Q1 fuel hedge is being unwound with a forecast loss of Rp 644 billion (RM 180 million) as Brent backwardation pushed realised versus hedged divergence to USD 22/bbl; (2) the new ASEAN open-skies allocation has handed slots on the regional capital–the regional capital, the regional capital–Singapore and the regional capital–Phuket trunk routes to competitors — yield erosion of 8-12% is projected on 14 routes; (3) the cabin-crew union filed a dispute over rostering and Hari Raya peak pay 18 days before the festive season, creating industrial-action risk on the 12 highest-yield days of the year. The Group Managing Director needs an ExCo pack in 10 days covering the fuel-hedge cash burn, network-restructuring response, CAAM/DGCA/MAVCOM regulator pack, and cabin-crew negotiation brief. Reference frame: comparable ASEAN full-service and low-cost airline groups, with CAAM, DGCA Indonesia, MAVCOM and IATA active concurrently.',
