      geo: 'MY+ID',
      companyBM: 'Zava Power',
      taglineBM: 'Pembaharuan PPA pada tarif lebih rendah mengancam EBITDA RM 240 juta + tarikh akhir arang batu-ke-tenaga boleh baharu 2030 + ganti rugi jumlah tertentu ketersediaan grid — Lembaga Pengarah dalam 21 hari.',
      scenarioBM: 'Zava Power ialah pengeluar tenaga bebas ASEAN dengan portfolio kasar 4.2 GW merentasi arang batu, gas kitar gabungan, solar berskala besar, hidro dan angin atas grid di Malaysia dan Indonesia. Kumpulan beroperasi di bawah Perjanjian Pembelian Tenaga (PPA) jangka panjang dengan off-taker utiliti nasional utama di kedua-dua negara. Tiga tekanan bertembung: (1) PPA arang batu terbesar (1,200 MW) akan diperbaharui dalam 14 bulan pada struktur tarif yang, di bawah rangka kerja kos tersamarata yang dikenakan pengawal selia, mengancam EBITDA FY2027 sebanyak RM 240 juta; (2) Energy Commission Malaysia (Suruhanjaya Tenaga / ST) telah menetapkan tarikh akhir peralihan arang batu-ke-tenaga boleh baharu menjelang 2030, memerlukan penyusunan semula keutamaan capex RM 2.1 bilion merentasi pipeline BESS, solar berskala besar dan angin atas grid; (3) dua insiden ketersediaan grid di loji Pasir Gudang dan Cilegon mencetuskan tuntutan ganti rugi jumlah tertentu daripada off-taker berjumlah RM 38 juta YTD serta tambahan RM 22 juta kontingen. Pengarah Urusan Kumpulan memerlukan pek Lembaga Pengarah dalam 21 hari merangkumi model pembaharuan PPA, program pemulihan ketersediaan loji, jadual capex arang batu-ke-tenaga boleh baharu, pek pengawal selia ST/MEMR/utiliti off-taker dan taklimat rundingan off-taker. Rangka rujukan: pengeluar tenaga bebas dan utiliti serantau yang sebanding.',
      companyIDEN: 'Zava Power',
      taglineIDEN: 'PPA renewal at lower tariff threatens Rp 859 billion EBITDA + 2030 coal-to-renewables transition deadline + grid availability LD — Board in 21 days.',
      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Power is an ASEAN independent power producer with a 4.2 GW gross portfolio across coal-fired, combined-cycle gas, large-scale solar, hydro, and on-grid wind assets in Malaysia and Indonesia. The Group operates under long-term PPAs with national utility off-takers in both countries. Three pressures converge: (1) the largest coal-fired PPA (1,200 MW) is due for renewal in 14 months under a tariff structure that, under the regulator-imposed levelised-cost framework, threatens Rp 859 billion (RM 240 million) of FY2027 EBITDA; (2) Energy Commission Malaysia (Suruhanjaya Tenaga / ST) codified a coal-to-renewables transition deadline by 2030, requiring capex re-prioritisation of Rp 7.5 trillion (RM 2.1 billion) across BESS, large-scale solar, and on-grid wind pipelines; (3) two grid-availability events at the Pasir Gudang and Cilegon plants triggered liquidated-damages claims from off-takers totalling Rp 136 billion YTD with a further Rp 79 billion contingent. The Group Managing Director needs a Board pack in 21 days covering the PPA renewal model, plant-availability remediation programme, coal-to-renewables capex schedule, ST/MEMR/utility-off-taker regulator pack, and off-taker negotiation brief. Reference frame: comparable regional independent power producers and utilities.',
