            {
              instr: '**Cowork Runbook · Investment Council of Agents — Riverside Phase 3 · Step 1 of 3** (Convene the council). Pattern: Council of Agents. Category: Property · Contoso Land. Apps: Word · PowerPoint · PDF · Deep Research. Sample source files (attach via 📎 Knowledge): Riverside_Phase3_IM.pdf, Riverside_Phase3_TechDD.pdf, Riverside_Site_Plan.pdf.',
              prompt: 'You are acting as a council of AI agents helping Contoso Land assess the investment merits of the Riverside Mixed-Use Phase 3 development. For each role below, assume the role completely and produce a long, audit-ready interim report.  Roles: 1. Land Bank Analyst — deep analysis of land cost, plot ratio, GDV/GFA, demographic catchment, comparable transactions within 5 km, current absorption rates. Cite township masterplans where relevant. 2. Macro Strategist — assess macro regime (rate path, USD outlook, household debt, Fed stance), implications for mortgage absorption and pre-sale velocity, correlation surprises. 3. Construction Risk Officer — independent view across material risk (steel, cement, EUR/USD), labour availability, contractor concentration, weather-window scheduling, defects-liability exposure. Propose mitigations. 4. Stress Tester — structured scenarios (base / bear / bespoke shocks), kill-switch thresholds, sensitivity narrative, what would force a launch delay. 5. Compliance & Policy Agent — investment permissibility, planning-approval gate status, affordable-housing quota, set-aside release schedule, planning conditions, environmental disclosures.  Finally, analyse all interim reports for recommendations, evidence, assumptions and dissenting views. Capture every claim with traceability back to a section of the IM or DD pack. Tunggu persetujuan saya sebelum mengirim apa pun secara eksternal atau memposting ke channel.'
            },
            {
              instr: '**Cowork Runbook · Investment Council of Agents — Riverside Phase 3 · Step 2 of 3** (Synthesise the pack). Pattern: Council of Agents. Category: Property · Contoso Land. Apps: Word · PowerPoint · PDF · Deep Research. **Honest framing:** ',
              prompt: 'Assemble the council outputs into a Word memo titled "Riverside Mixed-Use Phase 3 — Investment Council Recommendation" with: - Cover page (one-line recommendation) - One section per agent (~1 page each) - Dissent register — anywhere two agents disagreed and why - Appendix capturing every traceability link  Save to /ContosoLand/Pipeline/Riverside_Phase3/Council/. Apply the "Confidential — Board Pack" sensitivity label. Tunggu persetujuan saya sebelum mengirim apa pun secara eksternal atau memposting ke channel.'
            },
            {
              instr: '**Cowork Runbook · Investment Council of Agents — Riverside Phase 3 · HTML Artifact Step** (Pipeline). Pattern: Model → Interactive App. Apps: Cowork · Word · Outlook · Teams · Tracker. Produces a **interactive HTML pipeline timeline** plus 4 parallel side-deliverables. **Honest framing:** The HTML is for review and demo; for production use, hand the data over to your BI team. This is Step 3 of 3.',
              prompt: 'Building on the Investment Council of Agents — Riverside Phase 3 runbook output above, now produce a **SELF-CONTAINED interactive HTML** artifact for executive review. Use the data from the attached files: Riverside_Phase3_IM.pdf, Riverside_Phase3_TechDD.pdf, Riverside_Site_Plan.pdf.  The HTML must be a single .html file with inline CSS and inline JavaScript — NO external CDN, NO external image, NO web fonts. It must open and function fully offline. Use a clean executive aesthetic (slate text, off-white background, accent colour from the source brand).  **The interactive HTML pipeline timeline should be:** Riverside Phase 3 development timeline — phase lanes (land bank → entitlements → design → presales → construction → handover) with milestone markers, RAG status pills, council-of-agents verdict per lane, and an "open issues" badge per milestone.  In parallel, also do all of these in one Cowork run: 1) Save the HTML as \'Investment_Council_of_Agents_—_Riverside_Phase_3.html\' to /Cowork/Artifacts/[YYYY-MM]/. 2) Draft a 1-page Word memo summarising what the HTML shows, the top-3 insights an executive should read first, and the recommended next step. 3) Draft an Outlook email to the executive sponsor with the HTML attached, a 4-bullet TL;DR in the body, and a request to confirm by [DATE]. 4) Schedule a 30-minute Teams review meeting for [DATE+2 business days] with the sponsor + 2 named deputies; include the HTML link in the invite. 5) Update the tracker workbook with a new row: date, UC, artifact link, owner, review status (Pending), and target close date. Tunggu persetujuan saya sebelum mengirim apa pun secara eksternal atau memposting ke channel.'
            }
