      scenarioIDEN: 'Zava Connect is an ASEAN consumer super-app combining an e-commerce marketplace (24 million monthly buyers), a ride-hailing and food-delivery platform (3.8 million monthly riders/drivers), and a digital wallet (18 million activated users) across Malaysia and Indonesia. Three pressures converge: (1) GMV growth slowed from 32% YoY to 11% YoY over the last 3 quarters, with 6-month cohort retention dropping 18 percentage points — the FY2026 plan is now exposed; (2) rider supply shrank 14% MoM ahead of the Hari Raya peak, with the top 5 cities showing supply-demand imbalance >2x and rider-incentive spend already 22% over plan; (3) take-rate compression from concurrent regulator scrutiny — ASEAN Central Bank on the digital-wallet side, ASEAN Financial Services Authority on the Indonesian e-money side, KPDN consumer-pricing investigation, MCMC on platform content — narrowed the contribution-margin envelope by around 120 bps. The Group Managing Director needs a Board pack in 14 days covering the GMV cohort tracker, rider supply heatmap, ASEAN Central Bank/ASEAN Financial Services Authority compliance brief, take-rate defence pack, and festive peak operations playbook. Reference frame: comparable regional marketplace, ride-hailing, delivery, and digital-wallet platforms, with KPDN, the Indonesian Communications and Informatics Ministry, the Commodity Futures Trading Regulatory Agency, and MCMC active concurrently.',
