              prompt: 'Building on the Policy Paper Drafting & Industry Guidance Mode runbook output above, now produce a **SELF-CONTAINED interactive HTML** artifact for executive review. Use the data from the attached files: REG_Policy_Existing_Library.xlsx, REG_Policy_Peer_Regulator_Scan.xlsx, REG_Policy_Industry_Consultation_Notes.docx, REG_Policy_Standard_Template.docx.  The HTML must be a single .html file with inline CSS and inline JavaScript — NO external CDN, NO external image, NO web fonts. It must open and function fully offline. Use the Group corporate aesthetic (slate text, off-white background, brand accent colour).  **The interactive HTML dashboard should be:** Policy Comparative Dashboard — top KPI ribbon (Peer Regulators Scanned, Material Shifts Identified, Divergences, Risks), middle comparative table with local position vs MAS vs SFC vs ASIC vs FCA vs SEC across 6 dimensions, side panel of links to source documents. Toggle EN/BM for label translation.  In parallel, also do all of these in one Cowork run: 1) Save the HTML as \'Policy_Paper_Drafting_&_Industry_Guidance_Mode.html\' to /Cowork/Artifacts/[YYYY-MM]/. 2) Draft a 1-page Word memo summarising what the HTML shows, the top-3 insights an executive should read first, and the recommended next step. 3) Draft an Outlook email to the executive sponsor with the HTML attached, a 4-bullet TL;DR in the body, and a request to confirm by [DATE]. 4) Schedule a 30-minute Teams review meeting for [DATE+2 business days] with the sponsor + 2 named deputies; include the HTML link in the invite. 5) Update the case tracker workbook with a new row: date, UC, artifact link, owner, review status (Pending), and target close date. Tunggu persetujuan saya sebelum mengirim apa pun secara eksternal atau memposting ke channel.'
