              prompt: 'I am working under a tight deadline and the work product needs to be airtight, so please be thorough rather than terse. Zava Group Procurement is awarding the Group HRMS replacement (3,200 headcount across MY/ID/SG) in 14 days and the Procurement Steering Committee Chair needs a single defensible vendor recommendation backed by a complete score-sheet and an audit trail. Here is exactly what I need from you. Produce a vendor-recommendation pack in one shot. Ground every part of your answer in the inputs that follow, and walk through them methodically rather than skimming. /RFP_01_HRMS_Tender_Document.docx (the tender requirements), /RFP_02_HRMS_Evaluation_Criteria.docx (the 1,000-point scoring framework), and the six vendor responses (Workday, SAP SuccessFactors, Ramco, Oracle, TalentBridge, Dynamics 365) in /RFP_03 through /RFP_08 — every response workbook has the same tab structure so cross-vendor comparisons are direct. When you reply, organise the output as described below so I can lift it straight into my deliverable without reformatting. (1) Compliance Matrix — vendor × requirement table marking each requirement Met / Partial / Gap, with the vendor sheet + row reference per cell; total Met count per vendor. (2) 1,000-Point Score Sheet — each vendor scored across the 6 criteria families in /RFP_02 with sub-scores and total, plus a one-line rationale per family per vendor. (3) Cost-of-Ownership Comparison — Year-1 + 5-year TCO in MYR per vendor including licensing, implementation, support, and Zava-specific change-management ramp. (4) Risk Register — top 5 risks per vendor with severity and proposed mitigation, evidence-anchored. (5) Recommendation Narrative — 5-paragraph recommendation, naming a primary vendor, a fallback, and the 3 hard questions the Committee Chair must put to the primary vendor in the BAFO round before signing. Tone: regulator-grade, every score traceable. Be specific, attach a citation or sheet/tab/cell reference to every quantitative claim, and if anything is missing or contradictory call it out explicitly with the question I should ask next so nothing slips before the deadline.'
