              prompt: 'Building on the Major Incident Postmortem runbook output above, now produce a **SELF-CONTAINED interactive HTML** artifact for executive review. Use the data from the attached files: Incident_Bridge_Notes.docx.  The HTML must be a single .html file with inline CSS and inline JavaScript — NO external CDN, NO external image, NO web fonts. It must open and function fully offline. Use a clean executive aesthetic (slate text, off-white background, accent colour from the source brand).  **The interactive HTML pipeline timeline should be:** Major Incident Postmortem timeline — detect / triage / mitigate / restore / learn lanes with timestamp markers, MTTD/MTTR meters, top-3 contributing factors, and a remediation-tracker card per action.  In parallel, also do all of these in one Cowork run: 1) Save the HTML as \'Major_Incident_Postmortem.html\' to /Cowork/Artifacts/[YYYY-MM]/. 2) Draft a 1-page Word memo summarising what the HTML shows, the top-3 insights an executive should read first, and the recommended next step. 3) Draft an Outlook email to the executive sponsor with the HTML attached, a 4-bullet TL;DR in the body, and a request to confirm by [DATE]. 4) Schedule a 30-minute Teams review meeting for [DATE+2 business days] with the sponsor + 2 named deputies; include the HTML link in the invite. 5) Update the tracker workbook with a new row: date, UC, artifact link, owner, review status (Pending), and target close date. Tunggu persetujuan saya sebelum mengirim apa pun secara eksternal atau memposting ke channel.'
